# A dynamically stored qualified int128 is not an array index

Verifies the plain-integer index rule reports a qualified `int128` value
instead of silently extracting its magnitude.

>>> source
let values: int[] = [10]
let source: int128 = 1mm
let indexes: int[] = [source]
let selector = 0
print(values[indexes[selector]])

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: an array index must be a plain integer, found `int128[mm]`

<<< exit
1
